# Project Rules

## Stack
- MERN (MongoDB, Express, React, Node.js)
- Frontend: React
- Backend: Express REST API

## Conventions
- Conventional Commits for all commit messages
- Functional components + hooks only (no class components)
- camelCase for variables/functions, PascalCase for components
- Environment variables in .env, never committed

## Notes for AI assistant
- Prefer explicit error handling over silent failures
- Keep components small and colocate styles

## Rules learned from FL profile settings drill
- Forms use react-hook-form + zod for validation — never hand-rolled validation logic or manual date parsing.
- Every form input must have a real <label htmlFor>, not just a placeholder — applies to every field consistently, no exceptions.
- New form components require tests covering the invalid-input and edge-case paths (empty fields, malformed input, boundary values) before being considered complete.